# Codex Desktop copies paths matched here after creating a worktree.
#
# The corresponding roots are locally excluded from the ordinary untracked
# payload in `.git/info/exclude`. This keeps multi-gigabyte generated output,
# extracted delivery packages, caches, and stale capture trees in the parent
# checkout. Normal untracked source and evidence remain visible to Git and are
# copied by Codex's ordinary worktree path. Tracked files remain available
# normally and do not need entries here.

# Preserve lightweight, source-like deliverables without copying extracted
# packages or ZIP archives from outputs/.
/outputs/*.md
/outputs/*.mjs
/outputs/*.json
